WEBVTT

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:17.870
I wrecked my car.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.680
Well, get in.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:30.000
And now, fellas...

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:36.440
hear that fine new platter by Nat King Cole. I'd rather have the blues.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.660
It's pretty silly

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:06.200
I feel so mean and wrought

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:11.110
I'd rather have the blue than what I've got

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:19.910
The moon is dark and gloomy

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.460
I don't know what

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:30.000
Good the wet has got me caught

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:46.700
I'll never have the blues than what I've got All night, I walk the city

00:02:46.700 --> 00:03:00.000
Watching the people go by I try to save the city, but all that comes out

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.690
is a sign...

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:08.420
Thumb isn't good enough for you. You've got to use your whole body.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:12.470
Guys, would you stop if I use my thumb?

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:19.460
No. What's this all about?

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:20.940
I'll make a quick guess.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.960
You're out with some guy who thought no was a three-letter word.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:27.200
I should have thrown you off that cliff back there. I might still do it.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.800
Yeah.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.020
Where are you headed?

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:32.590
Los Angeles.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.090
Dropped me off at the first bus stop.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.380
You always go around with no clothes on?

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.220
What's the trouble, officer?

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.660
Woman escaped from an asylum upstate.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.000
Young, wearing a dress.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.140
French Co. Seen anybody up the road

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.130
to fit the description? No, I haven't, officer.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.290
Okay, move on.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:13.100
Haven't seen a thing, officer.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:16.580
Oh, my wife's been asleep.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:27.600
All right, move on. Can I have my hand back now?

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:27.880
No.

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.590
So you're a fugitive from a laughing house.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.930
They forced me to go there.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:40.880
Took away my clothes to make me stay.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:42.050
Who?

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.730
I wish I could tell you that.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.960
I have to tell someone.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.800
When people are in trouble, they need to talk.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.320
But you know the old saying.

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:00.000
What I don't know can't hurt me.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:17.740
- This wheel doesn't feel right, it keeps pulling over.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.660
- Good evening, folks.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:19.700
- Check the right front wheel.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:20.450
- Yes, sir.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.910
- What'd you find?

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.950
- Caught in a spindle, was binding against a drum.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:47.950
- Oh, we must have picked it up

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.410
when we were off the road back there.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.200
- Yeah?

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.160
- The only thing I ever pick up

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:54.920
when I go off the road is poison ivy.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.210
- Thanks, kid.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.030
- Thank you.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.570
Would you do me a favor, please?

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:11.800
Wouldn't mind at all.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:16.770
Would you put a stamp on this and drop it in the mailbox for me, please?

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:17.610
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.030
Anything else, ma'am?

00:06:21.630 --> 00:06:23.330
Did you find out what was wrong with the wheel?

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:24.700
Oh, yeah.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.000
You picked up a piece of branch when you took that little trip off the side of the road.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:59.380
Aren't you? It's your pretty little car.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:09.100
I was just thinking how much you can tell about a person from such simple things.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:11.450
Your car, for instance.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.570
Now, what kind of a message does it send you?

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:17.960
You have only one real, lasting love.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.390
Now, who could that be?

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:20.960
You.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:28.750
You're one of those self-indulgent males who thinks about nothing but his clothes, his car himself.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:32.840
But you do push-ups every morning just to keep your belly hard.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.200
You against good health or something?

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:39.060
I could tolerate flabby muscles in a man and make him more friendly.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:44.160
You're the kind of a person who never gives in a relationship.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:46.700
Who only takes.

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:49.950
Woman.

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:52.600
The incomplete sex.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.520
What does she need to complete her?

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:57.510
Why, man.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.000
Wonderful man.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.480
All right, all right, let it go.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.800
That bus stop will be coming up pretty soon, and I don't even know your name.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:10.250
Forget I'm a loony from the laughing house.

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:11.770
All loonies are dangerous.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:14.140
Did you ever read poetry?

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:17.220
No, of course you wouldn't.

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:20.330
Christina Rossetti wrote love sonnets.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:23.090
I was named after her.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:24.220
Christina?

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:26.000
Yes, Mike.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:30.000
I got your name for the registration certificate.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:35.490
Mr. Hammer, get me to that bus stop you forget you ever saw me.

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:44.570
We don't make that bus stop.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:45.130
We will.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:54.290
If we don't, remember me.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:34.530
She's passed out.

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:36.210
I'll bring her too.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:39.110
If you revive her, do you know what that will be?

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:40.140
Resurrection.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.760
That's what it will be.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.400
And do you know what resurrection means?

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.600
It means raise the dead.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.000
And just who do you think you are

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.360
that you think you can raise the dead?

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:51.980
Put him in a car too?

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:56.660
Naturally.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:13.720
Hi, Velda.

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:19.760
Hi.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.160
You're never around when I need you.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.710
You never need me when I'm around.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:25.790
Patsy.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:26.790
Five minutes.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:27.650
That's all you've got.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:33.240
Hi, Flatfoot.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.440
Hi.

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:39.440
Three days ago, I was figuring I'd have to finance a new tux to bury the corpse.

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:40.610
Three days?

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:42.650
How am I doing?

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:46.920
You're doing all right.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:50.000
Couple of weeks, you'll walk out of here.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.940
Can you remember, Mike, how it happened, the whole thing?

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.330
I never thought I'd smell that again.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.280
Look at all the goodies.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:20.650
I have a cab.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:23.440
Mr. Hammer, you won't need the cab.

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:25.630
We'd like to ask you a few questions.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.750
That figures. See you later.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.110
- Why don't you come in? It may be a while. - I'll wait here.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:42.790
We're not getting very far, are we, Mr. Hamm?

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:47.620
Well, now we have most of the facts. All we need is a little more fill-in.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:50.550
I almost got myself killed and all he wants is a little more fill-in.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:53.550
- Is it too much to ask for your cooperation? - And make him try it again?

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:55.440
You'll be given full protection.

00:12:56.720 --> 00:13:00.000
Maybe we'll have better luck with some more elementary questions.

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:02.110
Your full name, please, Mr. Hammer.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:05.840
Michael Hammer, 10401 Wilshire Boulevard, Los Angeles, California.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.760
Now, just what do you do for a living?

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:11.020
According to our information, he calls himself a private investigator.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.780
His specialty is divorce cases.

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:15.120
He's a bedroom dick.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:17.400
He gets information against the wife.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:20.190
Then he makes a deal with the wife to get evidence against the husband.

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:22.180
Thus, playing both ends against the middle.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:25.580
Just how do you achieve all this? You crawl under beds?

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:27.730
Nothing so primitive.

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:30.000
He has a secretary. At least that's what I do.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:35.610
what he calls her. What's her name, Mr. Hammer? Velda Wickman. She's a very attractive young

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:41.410
woman. Real woobate. Lives like a princess. He sticks her on to the husbands, and before

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:45.140
you know it, he's got his evidence, and he's ready for the big squeeze. Who do you stick

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:52.270
on to the wives, Mr. Hammer? That's his department. All right, you've got me convinced. I'm a real

00:13:52.270 --> 00:14:00.000
stinker. Now, if that's all you've got on your minds, I'd like to get along home. Yes, I know. You're anxious to get back to

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:04.480
- Life's work. - You're free to go.

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:15.610
- Open a window. - Thanks for waiting, Pat.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:20.000
She was a cute kid, had the nicest way of needling a guy.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:23.880
There'll be a long pause before those characters get a line on who killed her.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:27.170
Law isn't fast enough. You could do it a lot better, is that it?

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:28.930
Now look, Mike.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.840
- Who do you think you are? - What's the pitch, Pat?

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.150
An ordinary little girl gets killed that rings bells all the way to Washington.

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:40.440
It's gotta be a pitch.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.130
I'll give you a bit of advice.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:46.280
Too many people like you have contempt for anything that has to do with the law.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.760
You'd like to take it into your own hands.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:52.340
But when you do that, you might as well be living in a jungle.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.720
I picked up a girl.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:56.310
If she hadn't gotten in my way, I wouldn't have stopped.

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:58.930
She must be connected with something big.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:04.210
Mike, why don't you tell us what you know?

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:08.200
And step aside like a nice fella and let us do our job.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:10.050
What's in it for me?

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:37.080
Hey Sammy, look my friend just returned from the grave!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.080
Hey, Mike!

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.080
Ha ha!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.060
Vavavum!

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:41.080
Ha ha!

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.120
I'm sure glad you're back, Mike.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.940
Like Lazarus rose out from the grave.

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:46.840
Now tell me, what happened?

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.840
What did you do, huh?

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.890
Did you drive too fast that new rod?

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:52.890
Where is it? Velda says you were going to pick it up.

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:54.810
Oh, there's nothing to pick up, Mike.

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:57.890
You ought to have seen that beautiful and pretty little rod of yours.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.640
All torn up, scrap.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:02.820
Never gonna go va-va-voom no more.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.040
Break my heart.

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:05.570
Anyway, you're all right now, huh?

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:08.000
- A little shaky. - A little shaky, huh?

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:09.320
And you know what we're gonna do?

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:12.290
We're gonna pick up a couple of cute little Greek girls.

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:16.740
What I mean, va-va-voom, ha-ha, pretty pow!

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:20.450
Forgot to tell you, there are some guys looking for you.

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:21.830
Asking a lot of questions.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:24.390
- What kind of guys? - Tough guys.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.030
Very tough guys, Mike.

00:16:28.030 --> 00:16:29.800
Ah, forget it, look.

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.530
I'm glad you're back. You look swollen and listen.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.850
And I'll see you tomorrow. Take care of yourself, will you?

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:39.540
Huh? Are you all right, Mike?

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:42.510
I don't know yet. Maybe not.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:53.660
Hey, Sammy! What does he mean, "maybe not"?

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:56.560
Who knows what he means.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.320
5-4-1-2-4.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:15.320
Mr. Hammer, whom you are calling, is not available at present.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:20.570
If you wish to leave a record of your call, please state your message at the sound of the tone.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:23.000
Hello, Mike.

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:24.850
Just checking to see if you got home.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.580
Please call me when you...

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:27.750
Builder?

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:29.110
I got you there.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:30.000
Are you all right?

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.140
- Are you sure why? - I'll be right over.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.720
- What did they want? - They asked a lot of questions.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:08.060
- What kind of questions? - Questions.

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:12.190
When you leave, tell Nick.

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:20.770
- What do you want me to tell him? - You know, just to hold a soft part of your arms as a meal.

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:25.920
He'll drop his car off tonight and pick it up in the morning.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:35.300
- What's in the folder? - A guy named Ray Diker called up while you were in the hospital.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:42.530
He wants to see you, and I thought you'd want me to check up on him.

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:54.880
- Answer it. - Mike, it's official business this time.

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:56.470
Maybe he'll go away.

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:08.360
Go ahead, don't mind me.

00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:15.440
I'm revoking your private investigator's license.

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:18.490
Also, your gun permit.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:26.220
If I catch you snooping around with a gun in your hand, I'll throw you in jail.

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:32.880
I don't think you'd like it in jail.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:39.730
- Who's Ray Dyker? - What do you do with this guy?

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:42.260
He was a reporter on the news, wasn't he?

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:46.160
He used to write a science column. Why did he drop out?

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:52.010
I hear your friends were over to question him, too.

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:54.480
I gotta say it, he's got a nose.

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:58.290
He can sniff out information like nobody I ever saw.

00:22:00.890 --> 00:22:04.610
- What else did you hear? - Couldn't find him. He dropped out of sight.

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:10.150
Science editor of a newspaper drops out of sight, and nobody knows why.

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:23.720
- If you know anything, you better tell me, Mike. - If I knew anything, I would.

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:28.610
Sure you would.

00:22:42.440 --> 00:22:43.840
You ought to tell him, Mike.

00:22:44.990 --> 00:22:46.010
Did Becker leave an address?

00:22:46.270 --> 00:22:48.810
Oh, somewhere over on Flower Street.

00:22:49.650 --> 00:22:52.330
But if I were you, I wouldn't go.

00:22:53.190 --> 00:22:55.150
That tape I made of you and Loverboy got lost.

00:22:55.530 --> 00:22:56.690
There goes your case.

00:22:57.450 --> 00:22:58.890
Call him up and set up another session.

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:06.570
Tell 'em you're sorry, you wanna make up for all the pain you gave 'em.

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:09.830
Give 'em some of that sincerity.

00:23:09.830 --> 00:23:12.570
Oh, what'd you find out about the girl?

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:19.800
Christina Georgina Rossetti, poetess, English, born 1830, died 1894.

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:23.730
Your Christina was being held in that hospital for interrogation.

00:23:23.730 --> 00:23:25.480
Who by, the feds or state?

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:28.380
That they wouldn't tell me.

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:30.000
What's the point of all this?

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.620
if it's any of my business.

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:36.180
She told me if I dropped her off at the bus station,

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:37.400
I could forget her.

00:23:37.400 --> 00:23:43.060
But if she didn't make it, she said, remember me.

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:50.640
So remember her.

00:23:50.640 --> 00:23:57.810
She's dead, but I'm not dead.

00:23:57.810 --> 00:24:00.000
Hey.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.110
- Remember me?

00:24:02.110 --> 00:24:07.020
- Yeah, I remember you from somewhere.

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:10.810
Weren't you supposed to call that fellow Mr.

00:24:10.810 --> 00:24:11.630
What's his name?

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:18.230
- Friendly?

00:24:18.230 --> 00:24:20.750
It's my name for him.

00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:23.200
Mr. Friendly.

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:25.240
He certainly was friendly.

00:24:25.240 --> 00:24:27.500
- Maybe he'll give you some of that nice dialogue again,

00:24:27.500 --> 00:24:28.680
that honey talk.

00:24:30.700 --> 00:24:35.670
That tape sure was nice.

00:24:35.670 --> 00:24:37.560
Do me a favor, will you?

00:24:37.560 --> 00:24:39.700
Keep away from the windows.

00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:42.360
Somebody might blow you a kiss.

00:25:49.550 --> 00:25:51.250
- 1:21? - Solid.

00:26:16.410 --> 00:26:22.470
- Yeah, how much? - Damn. Like always. Thank you.

00:27:06.040 --> 00:27:09.350
Drop the knife, drop the knife, drop the knife!

00:28:52.680 --> 00:28:56.280
- Yeah, what do you want? - I want in.

00:28:56.610 --> 00:28:59.960
- What's the big idea? Who do you think you are? - To make it sound good.

00:29:05.020 --> 00:29:06.650
- Make it sound good.

00:29:06.650 --> 00:29:07.940
- What's on your mind?

